*** Keywords ***
UE Reservation
    [Documentation]    !!! Can only be used in Test Setup (requirement of taf_ue lib) !!!
    ...                Configures given list of UE before making L3 Call.
    ...                Key steps:
    ...                                 - UE PC setup - UE config injection,
    ...                                 - UE require - connect to UE
    ...                                 - UE reboot - reboot ue using ute library or adb command (skipped if reboot=False)
    ...                                 - trial UE attach/deatach
    ...                         Args:
    ...                                 - ues: list of UEs from init file
    ...                                 - ue_reboot: should UE reboot be preformed during reservation,
    ...                                   defaults to False, other options: adb, ute
    ...                                 - access_point_names: dict pairing UE serial numbers and APN
    ...                                 - attenuator_info: THIS PARAM CAN ONLY BE USED WHEN USING `L3 Call on SuperCell`
    ...                                     info on the attenuator from init file; defaults to None
    ...                                 - attenuator_config: THIS PARAM CAN ONLY BE USED WHEN USING `L3 Call on SuperCell`
    ...                                     configuration of attenuator ports with attenuation values e.g.
    ...                                     config = {
    ...                                            "MRBTS-50109/NRBTS-50109/NRCELL-1": {
    ...                                                "Subcell-0": [
    ...                                                    {"antenna": "RMOD-1/ANTL-1", "port": 0, "OFF": 0, "ON": 0},
    ...                                                    {"antenna": "RMOD-1/ANTL-2", "port": 0, "OFF": 0, "ON": 0},
    ...                                                    {"antenna": "RMOD-1/ANTL-5", "port": 0, "OFF": 0, "ON": 0},
    ...                                                    {"antenna": "RMOD-1/ANTL-6", "port": 0, "OFF": 0, "ON": 0},
    ...                                                ],
    ...                                                "Subcell-1": [
    ...                                                    {"antenna": "RMOD-2/ANTL-1", "port": 0, "OFF": 0, "ON": 0},
    ...                                                    {"antenna": "RMOD-2/ANTL-2", "port": 0, "OFF": 0, "ON": 0},
    ...                                                    {"antenna": "RMOD-2/ANTL-5", "port": 0, "OFF": 0, "ON": 0},
    ...                                                    {"antenna": "RMOD-2/ANTL-6", "port": 0, "OFF": 0, "ON": 0},
    ...                                                ],
    ...                                                "Subcell-2": [
    ...                                                    {"antenna": "RMOD-3/ANTL-1", "port": 0, "OFF": 0, "ON": 0},
    ...                                                    {"antenna": "RMOD-3/ANTL-2", "port": 0, "OFF": 0, "ON": 0},
    ...                                                    {"antenna": "RMOD-3/ANTL-5", "port": 0, "OFF": 0, "ON": 0},
    ...                                                    {"antenna": "RMOD-3/ANTL-6", "port": 0, "OFF": 0, "ON": 0},
    ...                                                ],
    ...                                            }
    ...                                        }
    ...                                 - ue_network_modes: dictionary with pairs of UE Serial Number - desired network mode e.g. {"SN1234": "NR_only", "SN321": "NR_only}
    ...                                                     possible network modes: NR_only, LTE_only, NR_LTE (NR_LTE mode CAN NOT be used with any of the other
    ...                                                     two in case of more than one UE); defaults to ${None} (current modes set on UEs will be used)
    [Arguments]                         ${ues}
    ...                                 ${ue_reboot}=${False}
    ...                                 ${access_point_names}=${None}
    ...                                 ${attenuator_info}=${None}
    ...                                 ${attenuator_config}=${None}
    ...                                 ${ue_network_modes}=${None}

    Log Operation                       Starting configuration of UEs..
    cm.configure_ues                    ues=${ues}
    ...                                 reboot=${ue_reboot}
    ...                                 access_point_names=${access_point_names}
    ...                                 attenuator_info=${attenuator_info}
    ...                                 attenuator_config=${attenuator_config}
    ...                                 ue_network_modes=${ue_network_modes}

    Log Result                          All UEs configured properly

L3 Call
    [Documentation]    Executes L3 Call test on given list of cells.
    ...                         Args:
    ...                                 - called_cells: list of distnames of cells to be called (CONFIGURATION DISTNAME)
    ...                                 - duration: duration of data transfer test in Robot time string format
    ...                                    e.g. '1 minutes 42 seconds' or '1min 42s'.
    ...                                 - throughputs: dict with throughput and deviation values for all cells,
    ...                                    it is also possible to add optional key 'ues' with list of UE settings for each
    ...                                    of the cells or for a number of them, example of throughputs dict:
    ...                                    throughput_100MHz = {
    ...                                         '827736065':
    ...                                             {
    ...                                                 'throughput':
    ...                                                     {
    ...                                                         'downlink': '100 Mbits/sec',
    ...                                                         'uplink': '15 Mbits/sec'
    ...                                                     },
    ...                                                 'info': '-',
    ...                                                 'deviation': '90%',
    ...                                                 'ues': [
    ...                                                           {'serial_number': 'SN1234',
    ...                                                            'network_mode': 'NR_only', 
    ...                                                            'access_point_name': '5GSAWRO',
    ...                                                            'apn_settings_path: 'Network & internet,Mobile network,SIM 1,Access Point Names'}
    ...                                                     ]
    ...                                               },
    ...                                   throughput 'ues' args:
    ...                                   - serial_number: serial number of UE
    ...                                   - network_mode: desired network mode for UE, possible values depend on the chosen network_mode_switch_method
    ...                                     in configuration file, e.g. for 'adb' switch method (NR_only, LTE_only),
    ...                                     for 'secretcode' switch method (NR only, LTE only)
    ...                                   - access_point_name: name of access point to be used. In case where 'apn_settings_path' is provided
    ...                                     this APN will be set on UE. If not provided, the APN will only be used to select the appropriate
    ...                                     interface for starting data transfer.
    ...                                   - apn_settings_path: path to APN settings on UE, e.g. 'Network & internet,Mobile network,SIM 1,Access Point Names'
    ...                                     arg should be used together with 'access_point_name'
    ...                                 - protocol: data transfer protocol
    ...                                 - udp_buffer: monitoring data buffer
    ...                                 - attach_should_be_possible: True - expected behaviour is that attach will be possible to cell,
    ...                                                              False - expected behaviour is that attach will NOT be possible to cell
    ...                                                                     (for example when we check attach to blocked cell); defaults to True
    ...                                 - prepare_cells_to_call: True - the enviornment will be prepared so that only the called cell is notBarred and unblocked
    ...                                                          False - the enviornment will not be changed and L3 call will be performed as is; defaults to True
    ...                                 - tput_verification_via_btslog: True - throughput verification will be performed using btslog
    ...                                                             False - throuput verification will be performed using iperf; defaults to False
    ...                                 - ue_network_modes: dictionary with pairs of UE Serial Number - desired network mode e.g. {"SN1234": "NR_only", "SN321": "NR_only}
    ...                                                     possible network modes: NR_only, LTE_only, NR_LTE (NR_LTE mode CAN NOT be used with any of the other
    ...                                                     two in case of more than one UE); defaults to ${None} (current modes set on UEs will be used)
    ...                                 - ignored_cells_on_preparation: SHOULD BE USED WITH `prepare_cells_to_call` set to True!
    ...                                                                 list of cells CONFIGURATION distnames that should be ignored during
    ...                                                                 L3 Call not called cells preparation procedure and not be blocked/barred
    [Arguments]                         ${called_cells}
    ...                                 ${duration}
    ...                                 ${throughputs}
    ...                                 ${protocol}
    ...                                 ${udp_buffer}=4M
    ...                                 ${attach_should_be_possible}=${True}
    ...                                 ${prepare_cells_to_call}=${True}
    ...                                 ${tput_verification_via_btslog}=${False}
    ...                                 ${ue_network_modes}=${None}
    ...                                 ${ignored_cells_on_preparation}=${None}

    cm.configure_env                    logs_path=${logs_path}
    ...                                 ue_network_modes=${ue_network_modes}
    ...                                 attach_should_be_possible=${attach_should_be_possible}

    Log Operation                       Executing L3 Call Test using cells: ${called_cells}
    FOR    ${called_cell}  IN  @{called_cells}
        run keyword if                  ${attach_should_be_possible}
        ...                             Log Step             Performing L3 Call to cell: ${called_cell}, attach should be possible
        ...                             ELSE
        ...                             Log Step             Performing L3 Call to cell: ${called_cell}, attach should NOT be possible
        cm.make_l3_call                 called_cell=${called_cell}
        ...                             duration=${duration}
        ...                             throughput=${throughputs}
        ...                             protocol=${protocol}
        ...                             udp_buffer=${udp_buffer}
        ...                             attach_should_be_possible=${attach_should_be_possible}
        ...                             prepare_cells_to_call=${prepare_cells_to_call}
        ...                             tput_verification_via_btslog=${tput_verification_via_btslog}
        ...                             ignored_cells_on_preparation=${ignored_cells_on_preparation}
    END

    Log Result                          Successfully executed L3 Call test for all cells!
    [Teardown]                          cm.clean_up_env

Parallel L3 Call
    [Documentation]    Executes Parallel L3 Call test on given list of cells and all UEs reserved during Test Setup.
    ...                         Args:
    ...                                 - called_cells: list of distnames of cells to be called (CONFIGURATION DISTNAME)
    ...                                 - duration: duration of data transfer test in Robot time string format
    ...                                    e.g. '1 minutes 42 seconds' or '1min 42s'.
    ...                                 - throughputs: dict with throughput and deviation values for all cells, example:
    ...                                    throughput_100MHz = {
    ...                                         '827736065':
    ...                                             {
    ...                                                 'throughput':
    ...                                                     {
    ...                                                         'downlink': '100 Mbits/sec',
    ...                                                         'uplink': '15 Mbits/sec'
    ...                                                     },
    ...                                                 'info': '-',
    ...                                                 'deviation': '90%'
    ...                                               },
    ...                                 - protocol: data transfer protocol
    ...                                 - udp_buffer: monitoring data buffer
    ...                                 - ue_network_modes: dictionary with pairs of UE Serial Number - desired network mode e.g. {"SN1234": "NR_only", "SN321": "NR_only}
    ...                                                     possible network modes: NR_only, LTE_only, NR_LTE (NR_LTE mode CAN NOT be used with any of the other
    ...                                                     two in case of more than one UE); defaults to ${None} (current modes set on UEs will be used)
    ...                                 - ignored_cells_on_preparation: SHOULD BE USED WITH `prepare_cells_to_call` set to True!
    ...                                                                 list of cells CONFIGURATION distnames that should be ignored during
    ...                                                                 L3 Call not called cells preparation procedure and not be blocked/barred

    [Arguments]                         ${called_cells}
    ...                                 ${duration}
    ...                                 ${throughputs}
    ...                                 ${protocol}
    ...                                 ${udp_buffer}=4M
    ...                                 ${ue_network_modes}=${None}
    ...                                 ${ignored_cells_on_preparation}=${None}

    cm.configure_env                    logs_path=${logs_path}
    ...                                 ue_network_modes=${ue_network_modes}

    Log Operation                       Executing Parallel L3 Call Test using cells: ${called_cells}
    FOR    ${called_cell}  IN  @{called_cells}
        Log Step                        Performing Parallel L3 Call to cell: ${called_cell}, attach should be possible
        cm.make_parallel_l3_call
        ...                             called_cell=${called_cell}
        ...                             duration=${duration}
        ...                             throughput=${throughputs}
        ...                             protocol=${protocol}
        ...                             udp_buffer=${udp_buffer}
        ...                             ignored_cells_on_preparation=${ignored_cells_on_preparation}
    END

    Log Result                          Successfully executed Parallel L3 Call test for all cells!
    [Teardown]                          cm.clean_up_env

Start L3 Call In Background
    [Documentation]    Executes L3 Call test on given cell(s) in background. This KW have two strategies:
    ...                1) Using ${called_cell} to execute L3 Call on SINGLE cell
    ...                2) Using ${cells_to_ues} to execute L3 Call on pairs of selected cells and UEs (please remember
    ...                   that given UE cannot occur more than once in ${cells_to_ues} dict)
    ...                Use 'Verify Background L3 Call Results' KW to collect L3 Call procedure results and clean up env.
    ...                Might either be executed with ${prepare_cells_to_call}=${True} (default value) - rest of the cells
    ...                will be barred before L3 call procedure or ${prepare_cells_to_call}=${False} - attach will be
    ...                performed without any changes for the rest of the cells.
    ...                         Args:
    ...                                 - called_cell: distname of cell to be called (CONFIGURATION DISTNAME)
    ...                                 - cells_to_ues: pairs of configuration distnames of cells and serial numbers of
    ...                                     UEs that will be attached to this cell e.g
    ...                                     {"MRBTS-1/NRCELL-1": "SN1234", "MRBTS-1/LNCEL-1": "SN432"}
    ...                                 - direction: direction in which data transfer should be performed, 'DL', 'UL' or 'UL_DL'
    ...                                 - duration: duration of data transfer test
    ...                                 - throughputs: dict with throughput and deviation values for all cells, example:
    ...                                    throughput_100MHz = {
    ...                                         '827736065':
    ...                                             {
    ...                                                 'throughput':
    ...                                                     {
    ...                                                         'downlink': '100 Mbits/sec',
    ...                                                         'uplink': '15 Mbits/sec'
    ...                                                     },
    ...                                                 'info': '-',
    ...                                                 'deviation': '90%'
    ...                                               },
    ...                                 - protocol: data transfer protocol
    ...                                 - udp_buffer: monitoring data buffer
    ...                                 - linux_congestion: option "-Z" for iperf2. TCP congestion algorithm (Linux and FreeBSD only) 
    ...                                                     to check supported algorithms use `sysctl net.ipv4.tcp_available_congestion_control` command
    ...                                 - prepare_cells_to_call: True - the enviornment will be prepared so that only the called cells are notBarred and unblocked
    ...                                                          False - the enviornment will not be changed and L3 call will be performed as is; defaults to True
    ...                                 - ue_network_modes: dictionary with pairs of UE Serial Number - desired network mode e.g. {"SN1234": "NR_only", "SN321": "NR_only}
    ...                                                     possible network modes: NR_only, LTE_only, NR_LTE (NR_LTE mode CAN NOT be used with any of the other
    ...                                                     two in case of more than one UE); defaults to ${None} (current modes set on UEs will be used)
    ...                                 - ignored_cells_on_preparation: SHOULD BE USED WITH `prepare_cells_to_call` set to True!
    ...                                                                 list of cells CONFIGURATION distnames that should be ignored during
    ...                                                                 L3 Call not called cells preparation procedure and not be blocked/barred
    [Arguments]                         ${direction}
    ...                                 ${duration}
    ...                                 ${throughputs}
    ...                                 ${protocol}
    ...                                 ${called_cell}=${None}
    ...                                 ${cells_to_ues}=${None}
    ...                                 ${udp_buffer}=4M
    ...                                 ${linux_congestion}=${None}
    ...                                 ${prepare_cells_to_call}=${True}
    ...                                 ${ue_network_modes}=${None}
    ...                                 ${ignored_cells_on_preparation}=${None}

    cm.configure_env                    logs_path=${logs_path}
    ...                                 ue_network_modes=${ue_network_modes}

    Run Keyword If                      '${called_cell}'!='${None}'
    ...                                 Log Operation
    ...                                 Starting background L3 Call to cell: ${called_cell}, attach should be possible
    ...                                 ELSE
    ...                                 Log Operation
    ...                                 Starting background L3 Call Test using pairs: ${cells_to_ues}

    ${procedure_status}                 Run Keyword And Return Status        cm.start_data_transfer_in_background
    ...                                 called_cell=${called_cell}
    ...                                 cells_to_ues=${cells_to_ues}
    ...                                 direction=${direction}
    ...                                 duration=${duration}
    ...                                 throughput=${throughputs}
    ...                                 protocol=${protocol}
    ...                                 udp_buffer=${udp_buffer}
    ...                                 linux_congestion=${linux_congestion}
    ...                                 prepare_cells_to_call=${prepare_cells_to_call}
    ...                                 ignored_cells_on_preparation=${ignored_cells_on_preparation}

    [Teardown]                          Run Keyword If      not ${procedure_status}   
    ...                                 Run Keywords
    ...                                 cm.clean_up_env
    ...                                 AND
    ...                                 Fail  Error occured when trying to execute background L3 call procedure. Please check 'start_data_transfer_in_background' method results in logs.

Verify Background L3 Call Results
    [Documentation]    Collects results from background L3 Call test on given cell. This KW have two strategies:
    ...                1) Use ${called_cell} arg if it was passed previously to 'Start L3 Call In Background' KW
    ...                2) Use ${cells_to_ues} arg if it was passed previously to 'Start L3 Call In Background' KW
    ...                Use 'Start L3 Call In Background' KW first to start L3 Call procedure in background.
    ...                         Args:
    ...                                 - called_cell: distname of cell to be called (CONFIGURATION DISTNAME)
    ...                                 - cells_to_ues: pairs of configuration distnames of cells and serial numbers of
    ...                                     UEs that will be attached to this cell e.g
    ...                                     {"MRBTS-1/NRCELL-1": "SN1234", "MRBTS-1/LNCEL-1": "SN432"}
    [Arguments]                         ${called_cell}=${None}
    ...                                 ${cells_to_ues}=${None}

    Run Keyword If                      '${called_cell}'!='${None}'
    ...                                 Log Operation
    ...                                 Waiting for background L3 call procedure to cell ${called_cell} to end...
    ...                                 ELSE
    ...                                 Log Operation
    ...                                 Waiting for background L3 call procedure to cells ${cells_to_ues.keys()} to end...

    cm.wait_for_background_data_transfer_to_end
    ...                                 called_cell=${called_cell}
    ...                                 cells_to_ues=${cells_to_ues}

    [Teardown]                          cm.clean_up_env

Get Average Throughput During Background L3 Call
    [Documentation]    Responsible for getting average throughput during background L3 Call test on given cell.
    ...                Average throughput is calculated without stopping the transfer.
    ...                Use 'Start L3 Call In Background' KW first to start L3 Call procedure in background.
    ...                Args:
    ...                    - called_cell: distname of cell to be called (CONFIGURATION DISTNAME)
    ...                    - cells_to_ues: pairs of configuration distnames of cells and serial numbers of
    ...                                    UEs that will be attached to this cell e.g
    ...                                    {"MRBTS-1/NRCELL-1": "SN1234", "MRBTS-1/LNCEL-1": "SN432"}
    ...                1) Use ${called_cell} arg if it was passed previously to 'Start L3 Call In Background' KW
    ...                2) Use ${cells_to_ues} arg if it was passed previously to 'Start L3 Call In Background' KW

    [Arguments]                         ${called_cell}=${None}
    ...                                 ${cells_to_ues}=${None}

    ${average_tput}=                    cm.get_average_throughput_during_background_l3_call
    ...                                 called_cell=${called_cell}
    ...                                 cells_to_ues=${cells_to_ues}
    [Return]                            ${average_tput}

Verify if Average Throughput is Within Deviation
    [Documentation]    Responsible for verifying if average throughput is within deviation for given called_cell.
    ...                Use of this keyword should be preceded by 'Get Average Throughput During Background L3 Call' KW.
    ...                Args:
    ...                    - called_cell: distname of cell to be called (CONFIGURATION DISTNAME)
    ...                    - cells_to_ues: pairs of configuration distnames of cells and serial numbers of
    ...                                    UEs that will be attached to this cell e.g
    ...                                    {"MRBTS-1/NRCELL-1": "SN1234", "MRBTS-1/LNCEL-1": "SN432"}
    ...                1) Use ${called_cell} arg if it was passed previously to 'Start L3 Call In Background' KW
    ...                2) Use ${cells_to_ues} arg if it was passed previously to 'Start L3 Call In Background' KW
    [Arguments]                         ${called_cell}=${None}
    ...                                 ${cells_to_ues}=${None}

    cm.verify_if_average_throughput_is_within_deviation
    ...                                 called_cell=${called_cell}
    ...                                 cells_to_ues=${cells_to_ues}

Stop Background L3 Call
    [Documentation]    Responsible for stopping background L3 Call test on given cell.
    ...                Use 'Start L3 Call In Background' KW first to start L3 Call procedure in background.
    ...                Args:
    ...                    - called_cell: distname of cell to be called (CONFIGURATION DISTNAME)
    ...                    - cells_to_ues: pairs of configuration distnames of cells and serial numbers of
    ...                                    UEs that will be attached to this cell e.g
    ...                                    {"MRBTS-1/NRCELL-1": "SN1234", "MRBTS-1/LNCEL-1": "SN432"}
    ...                1) Use ${called_cell} arg if it was passed previously to 'Start L3 Call In Background' KW
    ...                2) Use ${cells_to_ues} arg if it was passed previously to 'Start L3 Call In Background' KW
    [Arguments]                         ${called_cell}=${None}
    ...                                 ${cells_to_ues}=${None}

    Log Operation                       Stopping background L3 Call procedure without result verification...
    cm.stop_background_l3_call_and_verify_results
    ...                                 called_cell=${called_cell}
    ...                                 cells_to_ues=${cells_to_ues}
