L3 Call on Selected Cells using Selected UEs
    [Documentation]    Executes L3 Call on pairs of selected cells and UEs given by ${cells_to_ues} dictionary
    ...                L3 call will be performed simultaneously on all of the desired cells.
    ...                Might either be executed with ${prepare_cells_to_call}=${True} (default value) - rest of the cells
    ...                will be barred before L3 call procedure or ${prepare_cells_to_call}=${False} - attach will be
    ...                performed without any changes for the rest of the cells.
    ...                         Args:
    ...                                 - cells_to_ues: pairs of configuration distnames of cells and serial numbers of
    ...                                     UEs that will be attached to this cell e.g
    ...                                     {"MRBTS-1/NRCELL-1": "SN1234", "MRBTS-1/LNCEL-1": "SN432"}
    ...                                 - duration: duration of data transfer test in Robot time string format
    ...                                    e.g. '1 minutes 42 seconds' or '1min 42s'.
    ...                                 - throughputs: dict with throughput and deviation values for all cells, example:
    ...                                    throughput_100MHz = {
    ...                                         '827736065':
    ...                                             {
    ...                                                 'throughput':
    ...                                                     {
    ...                                                         'downlink': '100 Mbits/sec',
    ...                                                         'uplink': '15 Mbits/sec'
    ...                                                     },
    ...                                                 'info': '-',
    ...                                                 'deviation': '90%'
    ...                                               },
    ...                                 - protocol: data transfer protocol
    ...                                 - udp_buffer: monitoring data buffer
    ...                                 - prepare_cells_to_call: True - the enviornment will be prepared so that only the called cells are notBarred and unblocked
    ...                                                          False - the enviornment will not be changed and L3 call will be performed as is; defaults to True
    ...                                 - ue_network_modes: dictionary with pairs of UE Serial Number - desired network mode e.g. {"SN1234": "NR_only", "SN321": "NR_only}
    ...                                                     possible network modes: NR_only, LTE_only, NR_LTE (NR_LTE mode CAN NOT be used with any of the other
    ...                                                     two in case of more than one UE); defaults to ${None} (current modes set on UEs will be used
    ...                                 - attach_should_be_possible: True - expected behaviour is that attach will be possible to cell,
    ...                                                              False - expected behaviour is that attach will NOT be possible to cell
    ...                                                                     (for example when we check attach to blocked cell); defaults to True
    ...                                 - ignored_cells_on_preparation: SHOULD BE USED WITH `prepare_cells_to_call` set to True!
    ...                                                                 list of cells CONFIGURATION distnames that should be ignored during
    ...                                                                 L3 Call not called cells preparation procedure and not be blocked/barred

    [Arguments]                         ${cells_to_ues}
    ...                                 ${duration}
    ...                                 ${throughputs}
    ...                                 ${protocol}
    ...                                 ${udp_buffer}=4M
    ...                                 ${prepare_cells_to_call}=${True}
    ...                                 ${ue_network_modes}=${None}
    ...                                 ${attach_should_be_possible}=${True}
    ...                                 ${ignored_cells_on_preparation}=${None}

    cm.configure_env                    logs_path=${logs_path}
    ...                                 ue_network_modes=${ue_network_modes}
    ${attach_possibility_log}=          Set variable if      ${attach_should_be_possible}
    ...                                 attach should be possible.
    ...                                 attach should NOT be possible.

    Log Operation                       Executing L3 Call Test using pairs: ${cells_to_ues}, ${attach_possibility_log}
    cm.make_l3_call_on_selected_cells_using_selected_ues
    ...                                 cells_to_ues=${cells_to_ues}
    ...                                 duration=${duration}
    ...                                 throughput=${throughputs}
    ...                                 protocol=${protocol}
    ...                                 udp_buffer=${udp_buffer}
    ...                                 prepare_cells_to_call=${prepare_cells_to_call}
    ...                                 attach_should_be_possible=${attach_should_be_possible}
    ...                                 ignored_cells_on_preparation=${ignored_cells_on_preparation}

    Log Result                          Successfully executed L3 Call test on all cells!
    [Teardown]                          cm.clean_up_env

L3 Call on SuperCell
    [Documentation]    Responsible for executing L3 call procedure on each of the SubCells that make up
    ...                the SuperCell, keyword can only be used on configs that support SuperCell feature!
    ...                Args:
    ...                                 - called_supercell: CONFIGURATION DISTNAME distname of supercell to be called
    ...                                 - duration: duration of data transfer test in Robot time string format
    ...                                    e.g. '1 minutes 42 seconds' or '1min 42s'.
    ...                                 - throughputs: dict with throughput and deviation values for all cells, example:
    ...                                    throughput_100MHz = {
    ...                                         '827736065':
    ...                                             {
    ...                                                 'throughput':
    ...                                                     {
    ...                                                         'downlink': '100 Mbits/sec',
    ...                                                         'uplink': '15 Mbits/sec'
    ...                                                     },
    ...                                                 'info': '-',
    ...                                                 'deviation': '90%'
    ...                                               },
    ...                                 - protocol: data transfer protocol; defaults to udp
    ...                                 - udp_buffer: monitoring data buffer; defaults to "4M"
    ...                                 - attach_should_be_possible: True - expected behaviour is that attach will be possible to supercell,
    ...                                                              False - expected behaviour is that attach will NOT be possible to supercell
    ...                                                                     (for example when we check attach to blocked cell); defaults to True
    ...                                 - prepare_cells_to_call: True - the enviornment will be prepared so that only the called supercell is notBarred and unblocked
    ...                                                          False - the enviornment will not be changed and L3 call will be performed as is; defaults to True
    ...                                 - ue_network_modes: dictionary with pairs of UE Serial Number - desired network mode e.g. {"SN1234": "NR_only", "SN321": "NR_only}
    ...                                                     possible network modes: NR_only, LTE_only, NR_LTE (NR_LTE mode CAN NOT be used with any of the other
    ...                                                     two in case of more than one UE); defaults to ${None} (current modes set on UEs will be used)
    ...                                 - ignored_cells_on_preparation: SHOULD BE USED WITH `prepare_cells_to_call` set to True!
    ...                                                                 list of cells CONFIGURATION distnames that should be ignored during
    ...                                                                 L3 Call not called cells preparation procedure and not be blocked/barred
    [Arguments]                         ${called_supercell}
    ...                                 ${throughputs}
    ...                                 ${protocol}=udp
    ...                                 ${duration}=30s
    ...                                 ${udp_buffer}=4M
    ...                                 ${attach_should_be_possible}=${True}
    ...                                 ${prepare_cells_to_call}=${True}
    ...                                 ${ue_network_modes}=${None}
    ...                                 ${ignored_cells_on_preparation}=${None}

    cm.configure_env                    logs_path=${logs_path}
    ...                                 attach_should_be_possible=${attach_should_be_possible}
    ...                                 ue_network_modes=${ue_network_modes}

    run keyword if                      ${attach_should_be_possible}
    ...                                 Log Step             Performing L3 Call to supercell: ${called_supercell}, attach should be possible
    ...                                 ELSE
    ...                                 Log Step             Performing L3 Call to supercell: ${called_supercell}, attach should NOT be possible
    cm.make_l3_call_on_supercell        called_supercell=${called_supercell}
    ...                                 throughputs=${throughputs}
    ...                                 protocol=${protocol}
    ...                                 duration=${duration}
    ...                                 udp_buffer=${udp_buffer}
    ...                                 attach_should_be_possible=${attach_should_be_possible}
    ...                                 prepare_cells_to_call=${prepare_cells_to_call}
    ...                                 ignored_cells_on_preparation=${ignored_cells_on_preparation}

    Log Result                          Successfully executed L3 Call test on each of SuperCell's subcell!
    [Teardown]                          cm.clean_up_env

L3 Call on IoT Cell
    [Documentation]    Responsible for executing L3 call procedure for given IoT cell on all configured UEs,
    ...                keyword can only be used on configs that support IoT feature and all configured UEs supported IoT cells!
    ...                Args:
    ...                                 - called_cell: CONFIGURATION DISTNAME distname of IoT cell to be called
    ...                                 - duration: duration of data transfer test in Robot time string format
    ...                                             e.g. '1 minutes 42 seconds' or '1min 42s'.
    ...                                             Defaults to 30s
    ...                                 - attach_should_be_possible: True - expected behaviour is that attach will be possible to IoT cell,
    ...                                                              False - expected behaviour is that attach will NOT be possible to IoT cell
    ...                                                                     (for example when we check attach to blocked cell); defaults to True
    ...                                 - prepare_cells_to_call: True - the enviornment will be prepared so that only the called IoT cell is notBarred and unblocked
    ...                                                          False - the enviornment will not be changed and L3 call will be performed as is; defaults to True
    ...                                 - ignored_cells_on_preparation: SHOULD BE USED WITH `prepare_cells_to_call` set to True!
    ...                                                                 list of cells CONFIGURATION distnames that should be ignored during
    ...                                                                 L3 Call not called cells preparation procedure and not be blocked/barred
    [Arguments]                         ${called_cell}
    ...                                 ${duration}=30s
    ...                                 ${attach_should_be_possible}=${True}
    ...                                 ${prepare_cells_to_call}=${True}
    ...                                 ${ignored_cells_on_preparation}=${None}

    cm.configure_env                    logs_path=${logs_path}
    ...                                 attach_should_be_possible=${attach_should_be_possible}

    run keyword if                      ${attach_should_be_possible}
    ...                                 Log Step             Performing L3 Call on IoT cell: ${called_cell}, attach should be possible
    ...                                 ELSE
    ...                                 Log Step             Performing L3 Call on IoT cell: ${called_cell}, attach should NOT be possible
    cm.make_l3_call_on_iot_cell         called_cell=${called_cell}
    ...                                 duration=${duration}
    ...                                 attach_should_be_possible=${attach_should_be_possible}
    ...                                 prepare_cells_to_call=${prepare_cells_to_call}
    ...                                 ignored_cells_on_preparation=${ignored_cells_on_preparation}

    Log Result                          Successfully executed L3 Call test on IoT cell!
    [Teardown]                          cm.clean_up_env

L3 Call on Selected IoT Cells using Selected UEs
    [Documentation]    Executes L3 Call on pairs of selected IoT cells and UEs given by ${cells_to_ues} dictionary
    ...                L3 call will be performed simultaneously on all of the desired cells.
    ...                Might either be executed with ${prepare_cells_to_call}=${True} (default value) - rest of the cells
    ...                will be barred before L3 call procedure or ${prepare_cells_to_call}=${False} - attach will be
    ...                performed without any changes for the rest of the cells.
    ...                         Args:
    ...                                 - cells_to_ues: pairs of configuration distnames of IoT cells and serial numbers of
    ...                                     UEs that will be attached to this cell e.g
    ...                                     {"MRBTS-1/NRCELL-1": "SN1234", "MRBTS-1/LNCEL-1": "SN432"}
    ...                                 - duration: duration of data transfer test in Robot time string format
    ...                                             e.g. '1 minutes 42 seconds' or '1min 42s'.
    ...                                             Defaults to 30s
    ...                                 - prepare_cells_to_call: True - the enviornment will be prepared so that only the called cells are notBarred and unblocked
    ...                                                          False - the enviornment will not be changed and L3 call will be performed as is; defaults to True
    ...                                 - attach_should_be_possible: True - expected behaviour is that attach will be possible to cell,
    ...                                                              False - expected behaviour is that attach will NOT be possible to cell
    ...                                                                     (for example when we check attach to blocked cell); defaults to True
    ...                                 - ignored_cells_on_preparation: SHOULD BE USED WITH `prepare_cells_to_call` set to True!
    ...                                                                 list of cells CONFIGURATION distnames that should be ignored during
    ...                                                                 L3 Call not called cells preparation procedure and not be blocked/barred

    [Arguments]                         ${cells_to_ues}
    ...                                 ${duration}=30s
    ...                                 ${prepare_cells_to_call}=${True}
    ...                                 ${attach_should_be_possible}=${True}
    ...                                 ${ignored_cells_on_preparation}=${None}

    cm.configure_env                    logs_path=${logs_path}
    ...                                 attach_should_be_possible=${attach_should_be_possible}

    ${attach_possibility_log}=          Set variable if      ${attach_should_be_possible}
    ...                                 attach should be possible.
    ...                                 attach should NOT be possible.

    Log Operation                       Executing L3 Call Test with IoT cells using pairs: ${cells_to_ues}, ${attach_possibility_log}
    cm.make_l3_call_on_selected_iot_cells_using_selected_ues
    ...                                 cells_to_ues=${cells_to_ues}
    ...                                 duration=${duration}
    ...                                 prepare_cells_to_call=${prepare_cells_to_call}
    ...                                 attach_should_be_possible=${attach_should_be_possible}
    ...                                 ignored_cells_on_preparation=${ignored_cells_on_preparation}

    Log Result                          Successfully executed L3 Call test on all IoT cells!
    [Teardown]                          cm.clean_up_env

Perform UE Attach
    [Documentation]    Responsible for performing UE attach to given cell.
    ...                Args:
    ...                                 - called_cell: CONFIGURATION DISTNAME of cell to which UE should attach
    ...                                 - ue_network_modes: dictionary with pairs of UE Serial Number - desired network mode e.g. {"SN1234": "NR_only", "SN321": "NR_only}
    ...                                                     possible network modes: NR_only, LTE_only, NR_LTE (NR_LTE mode CAN NOT be used with any of the other
    ...                                                     two in case of more than one UE); defaults to ${None} (current modes set on UEs will be used)
    [Arguments]                         ${called_cell}
    ...                                 ${ue_network_modes}=${None}

    cm.configure_env                    logs_path=${logs_path}

    ${procedure_status}                 Run Keyword And Return Status
    ...                                 cm.perform_ue_attach
    ...                                 called_cell=${called_cell}
    ...                                 ue_network_modes=${ue_network_modes}

    Log Result                          Successfully performed UE attach to cell: ${called_cell}!
    [Teardown]                          Run Keyword If   not ${procedure_status}   
    ...                                 Run Keywords
    ...                                 cm.clean_up_env
    ...                                 AND
    ...                                 Fail  Error occured when trying to attach to cell: ${called_cell}.

Perform UE Detach
    [Documentation]    Responsible for performing UE detach from given cell. This method can only be called after executing
    ...                'Perform UE Attach' method on the same cell.
    ...                Args:
    ...                                 - called_cell: CONFIGURATION DISTNAME of cell from which UE should detach
    [Arguments]                         ${called_cell}

    cm.perform_ue_detach                called_cell=${called_cell}

    Log Result                          Successfully performed UE detach from cell: ${called_cell}!
    [Teardown]                          cm.clean_up_env

Clean Up Environment
    [Documentation]    Responsible for cleaning up the environment after finished execution of L3 Call
    ...                in particular responsible for unblocking and unbarring all cells, closing admin and smod connections
    ...                and deleting Env() instance.
    Log Operation      Starting environment cleanup...
    cm.clean_up_env

    Log Result         Environment cleanup operation complete!
